# s2b-port-forwards core wiring

## 1. Dependency edges
None: mixdog-connections already depends on mixdog-ssh, mixdog-app-protocol, async-trait, tokio (rt, sync, macros, time), tracing.
(The tunnel's own mixdog-ssh -> mixdog-workspace edge is in s2b-tunnel.wire.)

## 2. Modules
lib.rs of mixdog-connections already lists `pub mod port_forwards;`; the test module is declared inside port_forwards.rs.

## 3. SERVICE_PENDING
No protocol method is served by this module; nothing to remove.

## 4. For the link / service task
`ServerPortForwards::new(env, ctx_source, host_id, store)`: ctx_source is `ContextSource` = `Arc<dyn Fn() -> (SshTarget, Option<AttemptContext>)>`
(the server's ssh target and settings, read at every forward start). A ServerLink implements `port_forwards::PortsSource` (a watch of the
`ports` scoped feed list, created holding the first scan) and calls `forwards.follow(&link)`; on reattach it calls `restore()`; when the
server window closes it calls `close_all()`. Panel errors are `PortError` (Display: `<code>: <message>`).
